# The doorbell: someone rang while you're home. One line at once (with the
# parcel due today, when there is one). With a lock home.ini lets unlock
# (setup never writes that: you add unlock to its allow line by hand), the
# line asks [Unlock the door] [Leave it]: your tap is your own request,
# that one call fixed below, asked as every guarded call is; no answer in
# 10 minutes, nothing happens. Nothing unlocks by itself, and no camera is
# used. While you're away, triggers.ini's doorbell-away-... says it at
# once instead, through quiet hours, with no unlock.
workflow doorbell
subject house
about When someone rings while you're home: says so at once<doorbell words>.
start <bell starts>
tag no
limits steps 10, days 1
#if unlock

step ask
approve Someone's at {input}{event.hint}.
yes Unlock the door
no Leave it
timeout 10m
on deny goto left

step unlock
tool home/home_guarded {"device": "<unlock>", "action": "unlock"}
on fail goto failed
if unlock starts done goto unlocked

step unsure
say I sent it, but the <unlock label> hasn't said it is unlocked: {unlock}
end

step unlocked
say <Unlock label> unlocked.
end

step failed
say The <unlock label> didn't unlock: {unlock.error}
end

step left
end
#end
#if !unlock

step tell
say Someone's at {input}{event.hint}.
#end
